; Does cascade read back everything it writes, over generated input? No browser
; is involved: a value cascade accepted, printed, and then could not read is a
; defect whatever a browser thinks of the value.
;
; test/fixpoint asks the same question over the corpora the repo ships. This one
; draws from the seeded generator the accept-set harness uses, so the population
; moves with the seed rather than with the repository.

(executable
 (name readback)
 (libraries cascade cascade_spec_inventory fmt unix))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps readback.exe)
 (action
  (run %{dep:readback.exe})))
